   "text": {
    "L1": "Division undoes multiplication. Ask: what number times the divisor gives the dividend?",
    "L2": "For example, 4 times negative 3 is negative 12, so negative 12 divided by 4 is negative 3.",
    "L3": "A negative divisor is allowed. Divide the sizes, then use the signs: same signs give positive, and different signs give negative.",
    "L4": "So 12 divided by negative 3 is negative 4, while negative 15 divided by negative 3 is positive 5.",
    "L5": "Zero divided by any non-zero integer is zero. But dividing a non-zero integer by zero is not defined.",
    "L6": "For a worked example, ignore the signs first: 63 divided by 7 is 9.",
    "L7": "The signs are different, so negative 63 divided by 7 is negative 9. Check by multiplying negative 9 by 7 to get negative 63.",
    "L8": "Now choose the quotient of negative 48 divided by negative 6. Use the sign rule and check by multiplication."
   },
